    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Mold Plot Plugin is a comprehensive solution for managing &#8220;Plot&#8221; content types in WordPress. It introduces a custom post type for Plots and provides a set of Gutenberg blocks to display plot metadata effectively.</p>\n<p>Features:<br />\n*   Custom Post Type: Plot<br />\n*   Gutenberg Blocks: Plot, Plot Item, Plot Meta<br />\n*   AJAX-powered Featured Plot toggling<br />\n*   Integration with Mold Blocks (if active)</p>\n<p>Could be use to add image and text over any image as label or pin. add adds custom post type plot which contain detail information about the plot.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin files to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/wp-mold-plot</code> directory, or install the plugin through the WordPress plugins screen directly.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; screen in WordPress.</li>\n<li>Use the Settings-&gt;Mold Plot Blocks Settings to configure block visibility.</li>\n<li>After successful activation, you need to update permalink settings to make the plugin work properly as it uses custom post type permalinks(plot).</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id=\"does%20this%20plugin%20require%20any%20theme%3F\">\nDoes this plugin require any theme?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>It works with any theme, but relies on some shared styles if used with Mold Themes products.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>3.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Updated for latest WordPress versions.</li>\n<li>Improved security and escaping.</li>\n<li>Added Gutenberg blocks support.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Mold Plot Plugin adds custom post types and Gutenberg blocks for managing Plots.",
